{"id": "EUVD-2026-101049", "enisaUuid": "42d8e666-1cc5-3202-9b41-df839a180756", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/ipl: Fix NULL deref in kdump without re-IPL parm block\n\nSome IPL types, like HMC FTP boot or QEMU direct kernel boot, might\nnot provide an IPL parameter block. In this case, reipl_type_init()\nselects IPL_TYPE_UNKNOWN, and reipl_block_actual remains NULL.\n\nkdump passes the re-IPL parameter block to the dump kernel through\nos_info. Before commit 3b9678472bab (\"s390/ipl: correct kdump reipl\nblock checksum calculation\"), the os_info entry was added only for\nIPL types which initialized reipl_block_actual. That commit moved the\nos_info update to machine_crash_shutdown(), making it unconditional. As\na result, set_os_info_reipl_block() dereferences reipl_block_actual for\nIPL_TYPE_UNKNOWN. This may happen to work by chance when address zero\ncontains readable lowcore data and the resulting empty os_info entry is\nignored by the dump kernel.\n\nSkip the os_info update when no re-IPL parameter block is available.\nKdump then collect the dump and reboot without setting re-IPL parameter\nblock.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:26:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:18:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/030e88812435fc5d6aa42eee41fa77b5ea620327", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/92d0829eae257544b6b0faccb6e7079c45e22d48", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/50f9c40768e84f30d374235b3ee3850a94d9ac29", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6bf82bc5e00afaf836f8bb9a676bffc182a6bbd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f918871112e8e7c581e99eb8e545af4e59c8367"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v8v9-cp6p-qm5r", "CVE-2026-98400"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05d691d2-a4d8-3346-b8c8-8a4c604cc1f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.17"}, {"id": "0a365c51-9dd2-3773-aac3-d0ae3b5dd6f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b9678472bab86ae654cf2c18d5dd551558045be <b6bf82bc5e00afaf836f8bb9a676bffc182a6bbd"}, {"id": "0e4e9973-0246-3d82-925c-a9d5b447a12c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "1cded8db-b96f-33a0-a576-8fc99fdc00ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "29b2e391-511f-3d19-9a4d-9dacf043ad5f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b9678472bab86ae654cf2c18d5dd551558045be <50f9c40768e84f30d374235b3ee3850a94d9ac29"}, {"id": "2f0400ab-009b-3a8e-89c0-63d0ae758769", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "9039e072-06dc-3fba-808d-a86eacb2e8b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b9678472bab86ae654cf2c18d5dd551558045be <7f918871112e8e7c581e99eb8e545af4e59c8367"}, {"id": "9a8a63a6-f2b2-3a52-987f-22031a9c568f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "9fa9fe64-889b-338f-987f-c49af651b8cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "a4afcb80-eb09-3197-ab1b-a082aeeb6acc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b9678472bab86ae654cf2c18d5dd551558045be <92d0829eae257544b6b0faccb6e7079c45e22d48"}, {"id": "d344a7dd-0b5a-3376-9f9a-04c2a67cf072", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b9678472bab86ae654cf2c18d5dd551558045be <030e88812435fc5d6aa42eee41fa77b5ea620327"}, {"id": "ee25b4b7-8c4e-3665-b844-5aed3731af57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "00a83b20-5bc1-3d6d-883c-1888171edb12", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}